From 4ddac4dc2d28e5e832e4c73c420f1e2a14dcf1e5 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
Date: Mon, 28 Sep 2026 20:25:23 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 5/7] samples/bpf: implement RFS with socket hints and ordered
 CPUMAP

Add a runnable CPU steering policy on top of ordered CPUMAP. Observe
application socket use with BPF tracing and store an advisory CPU hint in
socket storage. Use the protocol send/receive entry points and successful
accept exit, plus TCP splice and optional zero-copy receive. Filter by the
loader's network namespace and established TCP/connected UDP state.

In XDP, hash the tuple to a stable domain before consulting the socket.
Read socket storage without allocating, release the lookup reference, and
select either the hinted CPU in the configured set or a stable hash
fallback. Lookup and allocation failures never switch an admitted tuple
to local PASS. Keep migration and completion decisions in the existing
ordered redirect kfunc; introduce no kernel policy or CONFIG_RPS
dependency.

Provide a libbpf loader with driver/generic XDP modes, CPU validation,
native RPS/RFS exclusion, initialization before attachment, and conditional
detachment after ingress quiescence and domain drain. Refuse replacement
of an existing program. Keep fixed domains and a static CPU set for this
sample; fragments, extension headers and custom demultiplexing remain
outside its ordering contract.

Build the sample out of tree with generated skeleton/header includes.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dong Chenchen <superdcc97@163.com>
